<description>
Return the single repeated tile from a grid made of two identical adjacent copies.

Input structure
- The grid is a rectangular pattern duplicated exactly once, either side-by-side
  or top-to-bottom.
- The two copies occupy equal-sized halves along the duplication axis.

Rule
- Find the only axis whose two equal halves are identical.
- Output the first half along that axis.

Key insight
- The output is not recolored or otherwise transformed; it is the source tile
  before the duplicate copy was appended.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "symmetry/pattern",
  "src": "entire input grid as two identical adjacent tile copies",
  "transform": "find the unique horizontal or vertical equal-half split whose halves match; output the first tile half",
  "grid_shape": "one repeated tile block"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  task: extract the single repeated tile from a grid made of two identical adjacent copies
  tile:
    rows: 2-5
    cols: 2-5
    colors: 3-4 distinct non-black colors (no color 0)
    not_self_duplicable: tile must NOT have equal top/bottom halves AND must NOT have equal left/right halves (ensures exactly one valid split axis on the input)
  input:
    construction: tile duplicated once, either horizontally (side-by-side) or vertically (top-to-bottom)
    horizontal: H rows x 2W cols (tile cols W is even or odd)
    vertical: 2H rows x W cols (tile rows H is even or odd)
    exactly_one_split: only one axis yields identical halves (guaranteed by not_self_duplicable constraint)
  output: the tile itself (first half along the unique split axis)

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first (build tile, then duplicate)
  steps:
    - pick tile dimensions H in [2,5], W in [2,5]
    - pick duplication axis (horizontal or vertical) randomly
    - pick 3-4 distinct colors from 1-9
    - fill tile randomly with chosen colors ensuring every color appears at least once
    - reject if tile has equal halves along any axis (both H and V); retry fill if so
    - construct input by concatenating tile with itself along chosen axis
    - verify exactly one split axis works on the resulting input (should hold by construction)
```
</generation_spec>
</reference_puzzle>

